TI  - Management of a large bronchopleural fistula using a tracheobronchial stent.
PG  - 57-9
AB  - Bronchopleural fistula, one of the most serious complications following 
      pneumonectomy, has a complicated treatment protocol and carries a high mortality 
      rate. We present a case report of a 75-year-old female with squamous cell 
      carcinoma of the lower lobe with positive peribronchial hilar nodes who underwent 
      a right pneumonectomy. She represented with a large bronchopleural fistula one 
      month postoperatively, eventually treated by a novel tracheobronchial stenting 
      procedure.
