DP  - 2012 Aug 27
TI  - Numerical analysis of airflow alteration in central airways following 
      tracheobronchial stent placement.
PG  - 23
LID - 10.1186/2162-3619-1-23 [doi]
AB  - The computational fluid dynamics method, which provides an estimation of the 
      pressure drop in the airway before and after the stent implantation, is proposed 
      in this study. This method is based on the finite volume model. The pressure 
      field was solved by the Navier-Stokes equations. The proposed methodology was 
      evaluated in seven health people (control group) and in fourteen patients who 
      were assigned in two groups, in which one was tracheal stenosis and the other was 
      bronchial stenosis. The results showed that the pressure drop after tracheal 
      stent implantation became significantly smaller. For bronchial stent implantation 
      cases, the airway resistance improved insignificantly.
