TI  - Tracheobronchial stent insertions in the management of major airway obstruction 
      in a patient with Hunter syndrome (type-II mucopolysaccharidosis).
PG  - 458-62
AB  - We report a case of a 22-year-old male with Hunter syndrome who developed 
      progressive major airway obstruction and was treated with insertion of plastic 
      and metallic stents, with dramatic improvement in the patient's symptomatic and 
      functional status. To the best of our knowledge, this is the first reported case 
      of endoluminal stents being used in the management of major airway obstruction in 
      a patient with Hunter syndrome.
